Subject: Cantor Semantic Coprocessor Identity

Description: The converged component identity joining Cantor direction, trusted compilation, semantic fabric, demand-loaded SOP operations, reflective execution, and replaceable model inference.

& [Identity] is the canonical architectural convergence
  + [specification_uuid] is a207a11d-c9f7-4e66-9e87-816c2e0706ff
  + [canonical_name] is Cantor
  + [canonical_role] is SOP semantic coprocessor
  + [status] is component_identity_authority
  + [purpose] is maintain and execute articulated semantic programs alongside a replaceable neural inference provider

& [CoprocessorRelation] is the functional pairing
  + [Cantor] is deterministic and inspectable semantic control, memory, retrieval, validation, authority, review, and state transition
  + [neural_model] is probabilistic language interpretation, association, synthesis, and candidate judgment
  + [pairing] is Cantor directs bounded inference calls and validates their proposed results
  = must: keep the model replaceable
  = must: keep Cantor able to execute exact retrieval, trust checks, validation, and state operations without neural inference
  = conclusion: from the application perspective Cantor is the model's semantic coprocessor; from Cantor's perspective the model is a probabilistic inference accelerator

& [InternalComponentMap] is the coalesced Cantor structure
  + [trusted_compiler] compiles signed SOP source into admitted packages
  + [recognition_gate] verifies Cantor Recognition Certificates, trust scopes, validity, and revocation
  + [semantic_fabric] stores typed nodes, relations, projections, source anchors, and activation overlays
  + [definition_service] resolves terms, contracts, operations, and perspectives
  + [query_microkernel] demand-loads the smallest applicable SOP operation bundles
  + [SOP_RVM] executes compiled reflection programs over externalized state
  + [history_service] supplies pertinent observations before material transitions
  + [review_service] forms inference capsules and tests candidates
  + [provider_adapter] translates bounded calls to Ollama or another model service
  + [effect_broker] authorizes and records external actions
  = must: expose stable interfaces among components
  = must: permit a minimal deployment to implement these as modules in one local process

& [CantorInputSet] is what the coprocessor accepts
  + [task_input] is preserved user or system material
  + [program_identity] is the compiled SOP reflection program
  + [runtime_state] is purpose, subject, attention, history, evidence, uncertainty, and budget
  + [authority_context] is caller permissions and obligations
  + [provider_capabilities] is the selected model adapter contract

& [CantorOutputSet] is what the coprocessor produces
  + [reflection_call_packet] is verified bounded context and operation for the model
  + [operation_bundle] is signed demand-loaded SOP guidance
  + [proposed_judgment_verdict] is accept, revise, reject, seek evidence, yield, fault, or escalate
  + [semantic_transition] is validated state change with provenance
  + [inference_capsule] is input, program, history, candidate, review, and revision lineage
  + [effect_decision] is authorized, denied, deferred, failed, or compensated
  + [reentry_state] is serializable continuation

& [CantorCycle] is the coprocessor instruction loop
  + [step_1] is accept task, program, state, and authority
  + [step_2] is resolve subject and pertinent history
  + [step_3] is demand-load signed SOP definitions and operations
  + [step_4] is construct a ReflectionCallPacket
  + [step_5] is invoke the selected neural provider when inference is required
  + [step_6] is validate ProposedJudgment against meaning, evidence, constraints, and authority
  + [step_7] is review and revise when required
  + [step_8] is commit an allowed semantic transition or broker an effect
  + [step_9] is append trace and advance, yield, fault, or complete

& [IndependenceBoundary] is what makes Cantor more than a prompt
  + [program_residency] is compiled SOP outside model weights and chat memory
  + [state_residency] is inspectable RuntimeState outside provider context
  + [source_authority] is cryptographically admitted packages
  + [provider_context] is disposable projection rebuilt for each bounded call
  + [provider_output] is an uncommitted proposal
  = must: restore work without relying on one model conversation
  = must: run the same fixture through mock and real providers

& [MinimumCoprocessorManifestation] is the only current implementation slice
  + [one_process] is a local Cantor executable or service
  + [one_package] is a test-signed compiled SOP package
  + [one_state] is in-memory externalized RuntimeState
  + [one_tool] is sop_query
  + [one_mock_provider] is deterministic
  + [one_subject] is resolved through two staged SOP queries
  + [one_review] is an inference capsule and verdict
  + [one_trace] is append-only
  = must: prove this before graph database, embeddings, Ollama adapter, faculties, distributed execution, or neural training

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable component-identity collection
  + [CSC-001] is identify Cantor as the SOP semantic coprocessor
  + [CSC-002] is identify SOP-RVM as Cantor's internal execution kernel
  + [CSC-003] is identify the neural model as a replaceable probabilistic inference provider
  + [CSC-004] is keep program, state, source authority, validation, and effects outside provider control
  + [CSC-005] is coalesce existing Cantor formations as internal component contracts
  + [CSC-006] is manifest the identity through one local process and one bounded fixture

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the coprocessor identity trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is Cantor as a local SOP semantic coprocessor paired with a neural model
  + [fold_2_boundary] is semantic control and state in Cantor; probabilistic generation in the replaceable provider
  + [fold_3_data_design] is package, program, state, query, bundle, call, proposal, verdict, transition, effect, capsule, and trace
  + [fold_4_governance] is signed authority, external state, proposal validation, provider replaceability, and effect brokering
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is resolve, retrieve, direct, infer, validate, review, transition, and record
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is Cantor-as-prompt, provider-owned state, duplicated runtime identity, monolithic premature implementation, and model-specific lock-in
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is component identity converged and minimum one-process proof bounded

